    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d966">

                <pb facs="1041" n="1029" sameAs="frus:frus1945v04/pg1029"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Control (Italy)/8–2145: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kirk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-24T18:00:00-04:00">August 24, 1945—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>774. Rome’s 2403, Aug. 21. Dept believes Udine should be returned to Ital Govt
                    with rest of North Italy unless prohibited by overriding military necessity
                    which could not be covered by arrangement Parri suggests.</p>
                <p>Would appreciate your appraisal of extent to which situation indicated in your
                    3333, Aug. 21,<anchor n="28" xml:id="d966-f1"/> and also Yugo demands during
                    Monfalcone negotiations<anchor n="29" xml:id="d966-f2"/> that special AMG zone
                    include Udine (your <pb facs="1042" n="1030" xml:id="pg1030"/> 2617 and 2624,
                    June 14)<anchor n="30" xml:id="d966-f3"/> may be influencing the decision to
                    retain AMG. Is necessity for retaining AMG in Udine upheld equally by US and UK
                    military authorities? Inform Rome.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
